## Overview{% #overview %}

The following tools are available in the Datadog MCP Server. Each entry includes the required toolset, permissions, and example prompts. Tools are grouped by toolsets, which allow you to use only the tools you need, saving valuable context window space.

{% callout %}

# Important note for users on the following Datadog sites: app.datadoghq.com, us3.datadoghq.com, us5.datadoghq.com, app.datadoghq.eu, ap1.datadoghq.com, ap2.datadoghq.com, uk1.datadoghq.com

By default, only tools in the `core` toolset are available. To enable product-specific tools, include the `toolsets` query parameter at the end of the endpoint URL you use to connect to the Datadog MCP Server. Use `toolsets=all` to enable all generally available toolsets (best for clients that support tool filtering to reduce context window usage). Tools in Preview are not included in `toolsets=all`.

For example, based on your selected Datadog site ({% placeholder "user-datadog-site-name" /%}), this URL enables only APM and Agent Observability tools:

```
<YOUR_MCP_SERVER_ENDPOINT>?toolsets=apm,llmobs

```

You can also exclude specific tools with the `omit_tools` query parameter.

{% /callout %}

See Set Up the Datadog MCP Server for more information on connecting to the MCP Server, enabling toolsets, and omitting specific tools.

{% alert level="info" %}
Datadog MCP Server tools are under significant development and are subject to change. Use this feedback form to share any feedback, use cases, or issues encountered with your prompts and queries.
{% /alert %}

### User-controlled content in tool results{% #user-controlled-content-in-tool-results %}

Some tools return content that users or monitored systems can set, such as tags, Docker labels, form responses, process command lines, and SQL queries. This content can include text that your AI agent might interpret as instructions. The MCP Server returns this content as data and does not run it, but it can't control how your agent interprets it. Review any actions your agent proposes based on this content, and grant only the permissions and toolsets your workflows need.

## Core tools{% #core-tools %}

The default toolset for logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, monitors, incidents, hosts, services, events, and notebooks.

### `search_datadog_events`{% #search_datadog_events %}

Toolset: core Permissions Required: `Events` and `Timeseries` Searches events like monitor alerts, deployment notifications, infrastructure changes, security findings, and service status changes.

- Show me all deployment events from the last 24 hours.
- Find events related to our production environment with error status.
- Get events tagged with `service:api` from the past hour.

Note: See the Event Management API for more details.
